# TEST_CASES — Behavior verification (Gherkin-style) + coverage

> **Purpose (L2+):** how correctness is proven — structured scenarios + a coverage
> matrix that maps scenarios → tests. Written in Phase 6, kept true after.

## §0 Anti-patterns (mandatory checks to always run)
- **Contract–route parity:** every route exists in `contracts/openapi/*.yaml`
  (`hasRoute()` guard). Tests must fail if a route lacks a contract entry.
- **Path on the wire:** use `:id` in code (Fastify) vs `{id}` in contract (OpenAPI) —
  mismatch breaks runtime. Guard catches it.
- **Timestamps:** `.toISOString()`, never `new Date()` (non-canonical).
- **Typing:** no `as unknown as X`, no `any`/`@ts-ignore`.

## Scenario — <Module A> · CRUD
```gherkin
Feature: <Module> CRUD
  As a client
  I want to create/read/update/delete <entity>
  So that <value>

  Scenario: create succeeds
    Given an authorized client
    When I POST /api/<module>/v1/<entity>
    Then the response is 201 and the entity has an id

  Scenario: contract conformance
    Then every route matches contracts/openapi/<svc>.yaml
```
> Coverage matrix:
> | Scenario | Test file | Green? |
> |----------|-----------|:------:|

## Scenario — Cross-module (SAGA)
```gherkin
Scenario: sagaN happy path
  Given storage and bus are up
  When <trigger event> fires
  Then <followers> run their step and the end state is <X>
```

## Scenario — E2E (L3·frontend-app)
```gherkin
Scenario: full flow
  Given an SPA is served
  When user does <X>
  Then the UI shows <Y>
```
> E2E compatibility — state the **number** of E2E tests and where (`services/frontend/test`).
> Keep it in the `docs/REFERENCE.md` drift table if inconsistent.

## Coverage matrix
| Module | Unit | Contract | Integration | Scenario (Gherkin) | Test files |
|--------|:----:|:--------:|:-----------:|:-------------------:|:----------:|
| <module> | ✅ | ✅ N/N | ⬍ (needs bus) | §Scenario | `test/*.test.ts` |

> **Rule:** coverage matrix must match the feature list in `FEATURES.md` 1:1. A
> scenario without a test is as bad as a test with no scenario.